Dragonbox is a float-to-string conversion algorithm: it finds the
shortest decimal representation of a binary floating-point number which
still rounds back to the same number.  It is based on Schubfach, by
Raffaello Giulietti, and also inspired by Grisu and Grisu-Exact.

This port installs the header-only dragonbox library, along with
dragonbox_to_chars, a shared library converting float and double values
into strings, and CMake package files for find_package(dragonbox).
